Colony {
  patterns: "Patterns"
  default: pattern "VimrcHTML" breadcrumbs "Home: //overview//"

  using: "vimscript.inweb"

  member: "overview"                                    to "" breadcrumbs ""
  member: "vimrc"      at "vimrc"
  member: "gvimrc"     at "gvimrc.inweb"                to ""
  member: "mail.vim"   at "after/ftplugin/mail.vim.w"   to "after/ftplugin/"
  member: "python.vim" at "after/ftplugin/python.inweb" to "after/ftplugin/"

  Page "overview" {
    Title: My Vim Configuration
    Notation: Markdown

    This is my annotated Vim configuration. And when I say it is my
    config, I mean it IS my config.

    It's written in the Literate Programming system
    [Inweb](https://ganelson.github.io/inweb/), and so it's compiled into
    both my actual `.vim` directory that Vim reads, and also into a
    human-readable version. viz. this website.

    ## Organization

    Conventions {
      commentary uses Markdown markup
    }
  }

  Navigation {
    <h1>[[Link "overview"]]
    <img src="[[Docs]]normalmode_logo.png" width=72 height=72">
    </a></h1>
    [[Menu "vimrc"]]
    [[Item "vimrc"]]
    [[Item "gvimrc"]]
    [[Menu "Filetype Plugins"]]
    [[Item "mail.vim" -> /after/ftplugin/mail.html]]
    [[Item "python.vim" -> /after/ftplugin/python.html]]
    [[Menu "Normal Mode"]]
    [[Item "Main Site" -> http://tiddler.local:8013/]]
    [[Item "Mastodon" -> https://mastodon.social/@normalmode]]
  }

  Conventions {
    commentary uses simplified markup
  }
}
